Guidelines for the 3-Minute Video Presentation (IDP)
1. Core Requirements
i. Time Limit: Your video duration must not exceed 3 minutes (180 seconds).
ii. Presentation Framework: Structure your video based on the NABC concept (Need, Approach, Benefit, Competition).
Please research the NABC presentation method online and refer to the attached supplementary file for more information.
2. Content & Production Tips
i. Focus on the Solution: Your video should clearly present your approach to the engineering problem, explaining exactly
why and how you solved it.
ii. Highlight the Prototype: Emphasize your final product and its working principles. Do not use this short video to document
the step-by-step progress of how the project was built; that detailed progress should be documented in your written report.
iii. Multimedia Integration: Ensure the video is visually and auditorily attractive and interesting. To achieve this, your content
should incorporate diverse media elements such as text, video clips, photographs, background music, and animations.
iv. Team Identification: You must creatively include your group members' pictures, names, and your official group number
somewhere within the video.
v. Be Creative: Remember, you only have 180 seconds to pitch your project, so try to be as creative as possible.
3. Submission & Publishing
i. Platform: The videos will be published online on YouTube.
ii. Submission Process: Please submit your finalized 3MT video to the IDP Coordinator, who will manage the uploading
process.
iii. Naming Convention: When filling in the 'BASIC INFO' and naming your video file, you must strictly follow this format:
a. Format: Video Title: MJIIT IDP 2026 GXX [Project Title]
b. (Note: "XX" represents your specific group number)
c. Example: MJIIT IDP 2025 G1 Energy Saving